<section class="section" data-link-id="1" id="home">
    <div class="wrapper">
        <div class="hero">
            <div class="hero-image">
                {#
                    Overrides three plugin defaults, all of which are wrong for
                    the one image above the fold.

                    formats drops png: the global list ends with it, and since
                    every browser supports png a browser without avif or webp
                    stopped there and took 937KB of lossless photograph, leaving
                    the jpeg in <img> unreachable. logo.svg still needs png, so
                    this is per-image rather than a config change.

                    loading and fetchpriority undo the global lazy, which was
                    deferring the LCP element.

                    widths follow the rendered width, not the box. object-fit:
                    cover on a square scales a 3:2 source by height, so a 250px
                    box paints 375px of image and a 375px box paints 563px —
                    doubled again for 2x screens.
                #}
                <img src="/assets/images/hero-bw.jpeg" alt=""
                    eleventy:formats="avif,webp,jpeg"
                    eleventy:widths="375,563,750,1125"
                    sizes="(max-width: 46.24em) 375px, 563px"
                    loading="eager"
                    fetchpriority="high">
            </div>
            <div class="hero-copy">
                <h1>I translate
                    <span class="hero-accent">visions&nbsp;
                    </span>
                    <br class="break-mobile">into
                    <span class="typewriter" style="color:#00808C">reality</span>.
                </h1>
                <p>I’m a full-stack developer in training, using AI to work across interfaces, application logic, and the systems underneath.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
